      "writtenOn": "2023-03-31T18:39:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is called upon unbonding. It is absolutely racey - in my opinion, unbonding should not touch the autoconnect list, it should be up to profiles to figure out if they are still interested in autoconnect. We also should not touch the behavior of 3P GATT clients from Java.\n\nBut this is a separate behavioral change that might break something, so I won\u0027t touch it. I also get that in practice, if you just unbonded from a peer, you almost certainly don\u0027t want to keep autoconnecting to it.",
